# Redirects for statically served routes.
#
# Like _headers, this file lives in the project root because
# @sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare requires it there and copies it into the build.
# Cloudflare Pages applies these at its asset handler, before a prerendered
# page is served, so they reach routes the Worker never sees.
#
# Two rounds of services have been retired. Without a redirect each URL becomes
# a 404, throwing away any link equity and dropping anyone who arrives from an
# old search result or a saved link.
#
# 2026-09-13: excavation, gravel driveway repair, drainage solutions and shed
# pads were retired when the company moved to land management. Excavation
# pointed at land clearing, which has since been retired itself, so it now lands
# on the services listing with the rest.
#
# 2026-09-21: land clearing, bush hogging, forestry mulching, trail systems and
# property maintenance were retired when the company moved to landscape
# maintenance and management. Property maintenance is the one with a real
# survivor — whole-property upkeep is now the comprehensive maintenance
# program. The other four have no equivalent, and sending them to a specific
# page the company does not offer would be worse than honest: they land on the
# services listing, which shows what the company does now.
#
# A test in src/lib/config/deployment.test.ts asserts every destination below is
# still a real route and every source is no longer a live service slug.

/services/excavation              /services                          301
/services/gravel-driveway-repair  /services                          301
/services/drainage-solutions      /services                          301
/services/shed-pad-preparation    /services                          301
/services/land-clearing           /services                          301
/services/bush-hogging            /services                          301
/services/forestry-mulching       /services                          301
/services/trail-systems           /services                          301
/services/property-maintenance    /services/maintenance-solutions    301
